## Understand Anything (codebase map)

This project uses **[Understand-Anything](https://github.com/Lum1104/Understand-Anything)** for architecture maps — interactive knowledge graphs with summaries, layers, and guided tours. It replaces the former **CodeGraph** MCP setup.

### Setup (once per machine)

```bash
./scripts/setup-understand-anything.sh
```

Restart Cursor after setup. Plugin auto-discovery uses `.cursor-plugin/plugin.json` at the repo root.

### When exploring structure

| Goal | What to do |
|------|------------|
| Build / refresh the graph | Agent: run **`/understand lib`** (Flutter app code only) or **`/understand`** (full repo) |
| Open visual dashboard | **`/understand-dashboard`** |
| Ask how something works | **`/understand-chat`** or read `.understand-anything/knowledge-graph.json` |
| Explain one file | **`/understand-explain lib/path/to/file.dart`** |
| Impact of local changes | **`/understand-diff`** |
| Business flows | **`/understand-domain`** |

### Agent rules

- **Prefer the committed graph** when `.understand-anything/knowledge-graph.json` exists — search nodes by `filePath`, `summary`, or `tags` before grepping the whole tree.
- **Do not use `codegraph_*` MCP tools** — CodeGraph is retired for this repo.
- **Scope large scans** to `lib/` (and `test/` if needed); skip `build/`, `.dart_tool/`, `*.g.dart`.
- After major refactors, suggest the user re-run `/understand lib` (incremental by default).
- For routing/UI audits, combine the graph with `docs/audits/` and manual navigation tests.

### Graph artifacts

- **Commit** `.understand-anything/knowledge-graph.json` (+ `meta.json`, `config.json`) for team onboarding; gitignore `intermediate/` and `diff-overlay.json`.
- See `docs/UNDERSTAND_ANYTHING.md` for full workflow.

### If plugin/skills missing

Run `./scripts/setup-understand-anything.sh` or add the plugin in **Cursor Settings → Plugins** → `https://github.com/Lum1104/Understand-Anything`.
